---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { business } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Preview Privacy Information" description="How this local M&H Construction design preview handles information. Production privacy details will be reviewed after hosting and lead handling are configured.">
  <section class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">DESIGN PREVIEW · OCTOBER 11, 2026</p><h1>Preview privacy<br /><em>information.</em></h1><p class="intro-text">This describes the current development preview. The production privacy policy will be prepared when hosting, inquiry handling, and any third-party services are confirmed.</p></section>
  <article class="container legal-copy"><h2>Project inquiries</h2><p>The preview form prepares an email using information you enter. It does not submit that information to a website backend, save it in browser storage, or send it automatically. You review and send the draft in your email app. Your chosen email provider handles that email.</p><h2>Phone and email contact</h2><p>You can call or email M&amp;H directly. Information you choose to share in those conversations will be used to respond to your inquiry and discuss your project. Retention and other production data practices still need to be confirmed.</p><h2>Tracking and external resources</h2><p>This preview includes no analytics, advertising pixels, embedded maps, third-party font requests, or tracking cookies added by the application. Assets are served locally. Development tooling and server logs are separate from the production website configuration.</p><h2>Generated images</h2><p>Interior photographs in this preview are generated design placeholders. They do not depict completed M&amp;H projects and will be replaced with approved authentic photography before launch.</p><h2>Questions or access difficulties</h2><p>Contact <a href={business.emailHref}>{business.email}</a> or call <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phone}</a> with questions or if you need help accessing information on this preview.</p></article>
</BaseLayout>
